    "metadata": {
        "title": "Bath Tub Cartridge Replacement",
        "last_updated": "July 26, 2024",
        "estimated_time": "30 minutes - 1 hour",
        "difficulty": "Moderate",
        "introduction": "This repair is needed to fix any water leakage in your bathtub or shower. The water is controlled by a device call a cartridge. When the cartridge is damaged, it becomes loose and begins to crack. Over time, these cracks let out even more water.\nThis guide will help you fix a leaky faucet, or any leakage of water that is occurring in the tub. This procedure is very safe, and the only hazard is slipping in the tub. The process is straightforward and can be achieved at home with the right tools. There are no special requirements for this guide.\nHowever, you will need to be patient, as parts of this guide will be frustrating due to the size of the tools being used. Replacing a tub cartridge will seem intimidating at first, but it is a lot easier than most would think. This guide will show you how to open up your faucet, find the cartridge, and replace it with a brand new one; doing so will fix the leaking water problem as well."
    },
